figdown 0.1 bitfield
# 0.1 (`QUOTING-RULES`): where the delimiter is WHITESPACE, a string-typed value
# is quoted — a bare token cannot grow into a phrase, and the old failure
# named the wrong thing (`unexpected argument "miss"` for a missing quote).
# Covers the positional labels, the `class` meaning, the classic `field`
# name, and the one string-typed OPTION value, `description=`.
bitfield x "X" numbering=msb0
field "Payload" 8
field "Payload2" 8 description=unquoted
field "Payload3" 8 description="quoted is fine"
